"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"`uniku/tsid`"},"326":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-74","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"\\~1.7 KB"},"327":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-75","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"`uniku/xid`"},"328":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-76","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"\\~2.1 KB"},"329":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-77","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"`uniku/errors`"},"330":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-78","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"\\~445 B"},"331":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-79","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"`uniku/generators`"},"332":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-80","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"\\~101 B"},"333":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-81","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"The CUID v2 entry point imports SHA3-512 from `@noble/hashes`, uniku's one runtime dependency; the size above excludes that external dependency's own weight. The UUID v5 entry point inlines its SHA-1, so its size includes the whole hash and it has no runtime dependency."},"334":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-82","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#reproduce-these-numbers","content":"Run the benchmark and bundle-size tooling from the repository root:"},"335":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-83","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#reproduce-these-numbers","content":"`bench:compat` runs uniku and the reference packages in separate processes; `bench:summary` reads those results and prints a comparison table. CI repeats the compatibility run four times with balanced launch orders. `bundle:summary` builds each entry point and reports its minified, gzipped size. `bench:cold-start` measures fresh-process startup separately from warmed generation throughput."},"336":{"id":"/docs","page_id":"/docs","type":"page","content":"Start here","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs"},"337":{"id":"/docs-0","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"Eleven type-safe ID strategies behind one API, with measured performance and independent entry points."},"338":{"id":"/docs-1","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#the-library-contract","content":"The library contract"},"339":{"id":"/docs-2","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"uniku collects eleven ID generation strategies behind one consistent, type-safe API: UUID v4/v5/v7, ULID, TypeID, Nanoid, CUID v2, KSUID, ObjectID, XID, and TSID. Published benchmarks compare generation speed with dedicated npm alternatives for each format. Each strategy still has its own entry point, so your application ships only the code it imports."},"340":{"id":"/docs-3","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Install uniku\" href=\"/docs/getting-started\" description=\"Generate your first ID in one import.\" icon=\"<PackageOpen />\" />"},"341":{"id":"/docs-4","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Compare eleven strategies\" href=\"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id\" description=\"Choose a format by the job it needs to do.\" icon=\"<ScanLine />\" />"},"342":{"id":"/docs-5","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"See the benchmarks\" href=\"/docs/guides/performance\" description=\"Compare every generator with its dedicated npm alternative.\" icon=\"<Gauge />\" />"},"343":{"id":"/docs-6","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Browse integrations\" href=\"/docs/guides/integrations\" description=\"Start with runnable Hono, Drizzle, and Effect examples.\" icon=\"<Blocks />\" />"},"344":{"id":"/docs-7","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Use the CLI\" href=\"/docs/cli\" description=\"Generate, inspect, and validate without writing a script.\" icon=\"<Terminal />\" />"},"345":{"id":"/docs-8","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Migrate to uniku\" href=\"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries\" description=\"Move from a familiar ID package without changing stored identifiers.\" icon=\"<ArrowRightLeft />\" />"},"346":{"id":"/docs-9","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#the-library-contract","content":"Every generator import returns a callable function with precise TypeScript signatures and the helpers that make sense for its format, such as `isValid()`, `toBytes()`, `fromBytes()`, or `timestamp()`. The library is ESM-only, built on web standards, and tested end to end across Node.js, Bun, Deno, browsers, and Cloudflare Workers. The stability contract defines the entry points, validation boundaries, and runtime support policy that take effect with `uniku@1.0.0`."},"347":{"id":"/docs-10","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#the-library-contract","content":"Install @uniku/cli when you need an ID in a terminal, migration, or shell pipeline. It shares the library's formats but has its own release lifecycle."},"348":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"page","content":"Migrate from other libraries","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Migration"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries"},"349":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-0","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","content":"Keep familiar formats while moving to direct, portable imports."},"350":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-1","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"From `uuid`"},"351":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-2","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#name-based-uuid-v5","content":"Name-based UUID v5"},"352":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-3","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-nanoid","content":"From `nanoid`"},"353":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-4","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-ulid","content":"From `ulid`"},"354":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-5","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-typeid-js","content":"From `typeid-js`"},"355":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-6","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-paralleldrivecuid2","content":"From `@paralleldrive/cuid2`"},"356":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-7","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-owpzksuid","content":"From `@owpz/ksuid`"},"357":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-8","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-bson","content":"From `bson`"},"358":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-9","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-tsid-ts","content":"From `tsid-ts`"},"359":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-10","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-xid-ts-or-nexid","content":"From `xid-ts` or `nexid`"},"360":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-11","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","content":"Migration is usually an import change first. Keep the stored identifier format stable, then move generation behind the new direct entry point. Every example below shows the value returned by the uniku generator."},"361":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-12","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"uniku generates UUID v4, v5, and v7. There is no uniku equivalent for v1, v3, or v6; keep the `uuid` package for those, or generate them elsewhere and only use uniku for v4, v5, and v7 values."},"362":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-13","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"The rest of `uuid`'s API maps onto uniku's per-generator methods, scoped to the version you imported:"},"363":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-14","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"`uuid`"},"364":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-15","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"uniku"},"365":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-16","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"`parse(id)`"},"366":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-17","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"`uuidv4.toBytes(id)` / `uuidv5.toBytes(id)` / `uuidv7.toBytes(id)` accept any UUID version, plus `NIL` and `MAX`. Unlike `parse()`, they validate only the length, the separators, and the hex characters — not the version nibble or the RFC variant"},"367":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-18","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"`stringify(bytes)`"},"368":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-19","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"`uuidv4.fromBytes(bytes)` / `uuidv5.fromBytes(bytes)` / `uuidv7.fromBytes(bytes)`"},"369":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-20","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"`validate(id)`"},"370":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-21","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"`uuidv4.isValid(id)` / `uuidv5.isValid(id)` / `uuidv7.isValid(id)`"},"371":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-22","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"`version(id)`"},"372":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-23","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"Implied by which `isValid` matches: each accepts only its own version."},"373":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-24","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#name-based-uuid-v5","content":"`uuid`'s `v5(name, namespace)` becomes `uuidv5(name, namespace)`, with the same argument order. The buffer form `v5(name, namespace, buf, offset)` keeps its order too. Both produce the same IDs for the same inputs, so stored v5 values stay valid."},"374":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-25","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#name-based-uuid-v5","content":"`uuid`"},"375":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-26","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#name-based-uuid-v5","content":"uniku"},"376":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-27","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#name-based-uuid-v5","content":"`v5(name, namespace)`"},"377":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-28","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#name-based-uuid-v5","content":"`uuidv5(name, namespace)`"},"378":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-29","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#name-based-uuid-v5","content":"`v5(name, namespace, buf, offset)`"},"379":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-30","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#name-based-uuid-v5","content":"`uuidv5(name, namespace, buf, offset)`"},"380":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-31","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#name-based-uuid-v5","content":"`v5.DNS` / `v5.URL`"},"381":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-32","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#name-based-uuid-v5","content":"`uuidv5.DNS` / `uuidv5.URL`"},"382":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-33","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#name-based-uuid-v5","content":"uniku also exposes `uuidv5.OID` and `uuidv5.X500`, and `uuidv5.namespace(ns)` to parse a namespace once for many names. See UUID v5."},"383":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-34","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-typeid-js","content":"`typeid-js` returns a TypeID object. uniku returns the canonical string directly."},"384":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-35","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-tsid-ts","content":"`tsid-ts` exposes a TSID object. uniku uses the native `bigint` as TSID's primary value."},"385":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-36","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-tsid-ts","content":"Convert at a string boundary when you need the canonical Base32 form:"},"386":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-37","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-xid-ts-or-nexid","content":"Both libraries implement the rs/xid representation. uniku returns the canonical string directly and does not require asynchronous setup."},"387":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-38","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-xid-ts-or-nexid","content":"Use `xid.toBytes(id)` and `xid.fromBytes(bytes)` when you store the 12-byte value."},"388":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-39","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-xid-ts-or-nexid","content":"Before replacing an existing generator, test the representation you store and expose. UUIDs, ULIDs, ObjectIDs, and XIDs have canonical byte forms; Nanoid and CUID v2 are string-native."},"389":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","type":"page","content":"Migrate to uniku v1","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Migration"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/v1"},"390":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-0","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/v1","content":"Prepare for the v1 entry-point contract without changing identifier data."},"391":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-1","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/v1#move-cuid-v2-to-the-versioned-entry-point","content":"Move CUID v2 to the versioned entry point"},"392":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-2","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/v1#update-error-code-matches","content":"Update error-code matches"},"393":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-3","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/v1#removed-codes","content":"Removed codes"},"394":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-4","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/v1#what-remains-stable","content":"What remains stable"},"395":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-5","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/v1","content":"uniku v1 keeps its canonical identifier formats stable while finalizing its pre-v1 entry points and machine-readable error contract."},"396":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-6","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/v1#move-cuid-v2-to-the-versioned-entry-point","content":"`uniku/cuid2` is a pre-v1 alias. Use the canonical versioned import before upgrading:"},"397":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-7","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/v1#move-cuid-v2-to-the-versioned-entry-point","content":"The generator behavior is the same. This is an import migration, not a data migration: existing CUID v2 values remain valid."},"398":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-8","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/v1#update-error-code-matches","content":"Pre-v1 error codes included the generator name. V1 uses strategy-agnostic codes and reports the generator separately through `error.strategy`:"},"399":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-9","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/v1#update-error-code-matches","content":"`uniku/errors` exports `ERROR_CODES`, the authoritative runtime catalog, and its derived `ErrorCode` type. The `_tag` classes and human-readable messages keep their existing roles."},"400":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-10","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/v1#update-error-code-matches","content":"This table maps every machine-readable code emitted by `uniku@0.4.3` to its v1 replacement:"},"401":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-11","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/v1#update-error-code-matches","content":"Pre-v1 code(s)"},"402":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-12","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/v1#update-error-code-matches","content":"V1 code"},"403":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-13","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/v1#update-error-code-matches","content":"`UUID_TIMESTAMP_OUT_OF_RANGE`, `ULID_TIMESTAMP_OUT_OF_RANGE`, `ULID_TIMESTAMP_OVERFLOW`, `KSUID_TIMESTAMP_TOO_LOW`, `KSUID_TIMESTAMP_TOO_HIGH`, `OBJECTID_TIMESTAMP